<title>HUNGARY: INDICATORS - Hungary - updated June 26.</title>
<headline>INDICATORS - Hungary - updated June 26.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The latest indicators:</p>
<p> GDP (prelim. pct)    1996 +1.0pct (Q4 3.0 yr/yr Q3 +1.0 yr/yr)</p>
<p> CPI (pct)		May +1.3 m/m +17.7 y/y  (Apr +1.4  +18.6)</p>
<p> PPI (pct)		Apr +1.3m/m +20.0yr/yr (March +1.5 +21.8)</p>
<p> Ind. output(pct)     Apr +9.0m/m +11.4yr/yr  (March -8.6 +3.3)</p>
<p> Current account	Jan-March -$477 million   (Jan-Feb -$498 million)</p>
<p> NBH trade deficit    Jan-March $402 million	(Jan-Feb $439million)</p>
<p> MIT trade deficit    Jan-April $907 million  (Jan-March $690 million)*</p>
<p> Gross foreign debt   March $24,442.5 million   (Feb $24,440.8 million)</p>
<p> Net foreign debt     March $12,570.3 million   (Feb $12,754.2 million)</p>
<p> Unemployment (pct)   May 10.6 pct		 (April 10.8 pct)</p>
<p> Budget balance (HUF) Jan-May -150 bln    (Jan-April -126.7bln)</p>
<p>T-bill yields% (1mo) 20.34 (3mo) 20.02 (6mo) 19.71 (1yr) 20.18</p>
<p>Government bond yields:(2-yr 1999/G) 18.42 (3-yr 2000/E) 17.42</p>
<p>(5-yr 2001/C) 15.41  7-yr bond avg price: (2004/F) 101.67 pct</p>
<p>The NBH is BBB by Duff &amp; Phelps and IBCA, BBB-minus by S&amp;P and Thomson BankWatch, Baa3 by Moody's Investors Service and BBB+ by the Japan Credit Rating Agency.</p>
<p>* The National Bank of Hungary's (NBH) March current account and trade figures are preliminary.</p>
<p>** The January-March and January-April Ministry of Industry and Trade and Tourism (MIT) trade deficit figures are preliminary and are likely to be reduced. NBH trade data are based on cash flow, MIT data on customs statistics.</p>
